   "unit_text": "Sensory epithelial hair cells (Fig. 25): The sensory hair \ncells are of two types: type 1 and type 2. From the \nupper surface of each cell projects a kinocilium and \nmultiple stereocilia. The kinocilium, which is thicker than \nstereocilia, is located on the edge of the cell. Sensory \ncells are surrounded by supporting cells which have \nmicrovilli on their upper surface. Hair cells of both types \nmay have contact with the same nerve calyx.",
